<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vaira Vīķe-Freiberga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1937</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vaira Vīķe-Freiberga is a Latvian-Canadian psychologist and politician who was president of Latvia from 1999 to 2007, the first woman to hold the office. Born in Riga, she fled with her family in 1944 and built an academic career at the University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a> before returning to Latvia in 1998. During her presidency Latvia joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a> in 2004.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vaira-vike-freiberga.jpg" alt="Vaira Vīķe-Freiberga" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Reinis Inkēns, Saeima · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VVF2022.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
